  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 102 AM EDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe unsettled pattern will remain across South FL for much of the \nupcoming work week. A broad upper level trough will remain over New \nEngland and the Mid Atlantic, with surface and upper level high \npressure over the west/central Atlantic. This will trap an area of \nenhanced moisture across South FL. With the low/mid level flow \nremaining westerly much of the week, this will result in above \naverage PoPs across the east coast metro each day. While the \nrainfall will be much appreciated given the ongoing drought, will \nneed to be on guard for the potential of urban and poor drainage \nflooding each day across the metro. \n\nTemperatures during the extended period will remain above normal, \nwith high temps generally in the low to mid 90s and low temps \nranging from the middle 70s over inland South FL to around 80 closer \nto the coasts.",
